 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# URAE Tutorial: Non-Euclidean Geometry & Hyperbolic Tessellations\n",
    "\n",
    "This tutorial explores Riemannian and Non-Euclidean computational geometry in URAE:\n",
    "- **Poincaré Disk Model $\\mathbb{D}$**: $ds^2 = \\frac{4(dx^2 + dy^2)}{(1 - x^2 - y^2)^2}$\n",
    "- **Upper Half-Plane Model $\\mathbb{H}^2$**: $ds^2 = \\frac{dx^2 + dy^2}{y^2}$\n",
    "- **Cayley Conformal Isomorphism**: $w = i \\frac{1 + z}{1 - z}$\n",
    "- **Gauss-Bonnet Defect**: $\\operatorname{Area}(\\Delta) = \\pi - (\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma)$\n",
    "- **Schläfli Regular $\{p, q\}$ Tilings**: M.C. Escher hyperbolic circle limits"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import urae\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create points within the open unit disk |z| < 1\n",
    "p1 = urae.noneuclidean.PoincareDiskPoint(0.2, 0.3)\n",
    "p2 = urae.noneuclidean.PoincareDiskPoint(-0.4, 0.5)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Exact geodesic distance\n",
    "dist = p1.distance(p2)\n",
    "print(\"Poincaré Geodesic Distance d(p1, p2) =\", dist)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Cayley Conformal Isomorphism from D to H^2\n",
    "uhp_p1 = urae.noneuclidean.UniversalBridge.poincare_to_upper_half_plane(p1)\n",
    "print(\"Upper Half-Plane coordinate (x, y) =\", (uhp_p1.x, uhp_p1.y))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Map back to D\n",
    "p1_back = urae.noneuclidean.UniversalBridge.upper_half_plane_to_poincare(uhp_p1)\n",
    "print(\"Roundtrip Poincaré point =\", (p1_back.x, p1_back.y))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Compute Gauss-Bonnet area defect for hyperbolic triangle\n",
    "alpha = 0.523598  # pi / 6\n",
    "beta = 0.785398   # pi / 4\n",
    "gamma = 1.047197  # pi / 3\n",
    "\n",
    "tri_area = urae.noneuclidean.HyperbolicTriangle.area(alpha, beta, gamma)\n",
    "print(\"Hyperbolic Triangle Area =\", tri_area)"
   ]
  }
 ],
